 "method": [
  "The window was resized to 460x1000 through the compositor (hyprctl), so the renderer received a real resize and the host narrow breakpoint ($narrowViewport, matchMedia max-width 639.98px) engaged. The earlier frame set used Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride, which changes innerWidth but does not deliver the media-query change to the host atom — those frames measured a wide layout squeezed into a narrow viewport.",
  "Text scale is emulated by setting the root font size to 200% (16px → 32px), which is how the plugin consumes rem tokens; it is not OS-level display scaling.",
  "View switching uses the plugin's own Textbook/Guided switcher; theme switching uses the host appearance.toggleMode keybind (Shift+X) and is verified against body[data-hermes-mode].",
  "routeWidth is [data-cb-route]; viewWidth is [data-cb-lesson-view]; horizontalOverflow is documentElement.scrollWidth > innerWidth + 1.",
  "The narrow chat overlay is closed before every lesson frame and opened only for 14-chat-overlay-dark-460px."
 ],
 "limits": [
  "The lesson rendered here is the pre-existing demo course served by the isolated backend; no provider was called and no spend occurred.",
  "The host change is committed on wt/host-narrow-rail in the operator's hermes-agent fork and was applied to the installed checkout only for the duration of the capture, then reverted. The 460px claim holds for the shipped app only once that branch is merged and installed.",
  "At 200% text the plugin's own header tab strip truncates its third label (\"Parent Stu…\"). That is plugin-side label truncation inside a 432px page, not host width allocation, and it does not clip lesson content."
 ]
